    "title": "Hypersingular Riesz-energy constants on surfaces from triangular-lattice universal optimality",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23202994",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-06",
    "description": "<p>This consequence note records the exact ordered-pair two-dimensional hypersingular Riesz-energy constant for every real s &gt; 2: C_(s,2) = zeta_Lambda(s), with Lambda the covolume-one triangular lattice. For every smooth compact embedded surface with positive area A, including smooth boundary and using ambient Euclidean distance, the minimal ordered energy is asymptotic to zeta_Lambda(s) A^(-s/2) N^(1+s/2). The unit sphere coefficient is zeta_Lambda(s)/(4 pi)^(s/2).</p><p>OpenAI's recently released planar universal-energy theorem is the substantive new input. The finite/periodic reduction and manifold universality are established results of Hardin, Saff, Simanek, Leble and Serfaty, with periodic averaging credited to Cohn and Kumar. We give a self-contained gap-periodization account with exact pair, density, covolume and tail conventions. The target is the dimension-two s &gt; 2 case of Brauchart-Hardin-Saff Conjecture 2, originally posed for the sphere by Kuijlaars and Saff. No independent base breakthrough or first-public-priority claim is made.</p><p>The upstream analytic arguments were independently audited and their finite certificates reproduced. Actual Lean source semantics were inspected, but a complete pinned Lean/Mathlib build was not reproduced; no formal-verification claim is made. AI tools were used extensively in research, drafting and verification. The preprint has not undergone conventional human peer review or refereeing at publication; automated adversarial audits are not human peer review. No microscopic crystallization, uniqueness of finite minimizers, new s &lt;= 2 result, other-dimensional constant or subleading expansion is claimed.</p>",
